@startuml ProximaDB Search Sequence
!theme plain
title ProximaDB - Polymorphic Search Sequence Diagram

participant "Client" as C
participant "REST/gRPC\nHandler" as H
participant "Vector\nService" as VS
participant "Search\nFactory" as SF
participant "WAL\nEngine" as WAL
participant "LSM\nEngine" as LSM
participant "VIPER\nEngine" as VIPER
participant "Dedup\nManager" as DM

== Search Request Flow ==

C -> H: POST /api/v1/vector/search
activate H
H -> H: Parse request & extract\nsearch parameters
H -> VS: search_vectors_polymorphic(\ncollection_id, query_vector,\nk, search_params)
activate VS

VS -> VS: Validate collection exists
VS -> VS: Build SearchContext with\nquantization hints

VS -> SF: create_search_engine(\ncollection, search_params)
activate SF
SF -> SF: Detect storage distribution
SF -> SF: Select optimal search strategy
SF <-- SF: SearchEngine instance
VS <-- SF: Polymorphic SearchEngine
deactivate SF

== Multi-Tier Search ==

VS -> WAL: search_unflushed(query, k)
activate WAL
WAL -> WAL: Scan in-memory vectors
WAL -> WAL: Apply metadata filters
WAL --> VS: WAL results + timestamps
deactivate WAL

VS -> LSM: search_recent(query, k)
activate LSM
LSM -> LSM: Search SSTable indexes
LSM -> LSM: Use bloom filters
LSM -> LSM: Apply metadata predicates
LSM --> VS: LSM results + timestamps
deactivate LSM

VS -> VIPER: search_compacted(query, k)
activate VIPER
VIPER -> VIPER: ML cluster selection
VIPER -> VIPER: Quantized coarse search
VIPER -> VIPER: Parquet predicate pushdown
VIPER -> VIPER: Fine-grained reranking
VIPER --> VS: VIPER results + timestamps
deactivate VIPER

== Deduplication & Merge ==

VS -> DM: deduplicate_results(\nwal_results, lsm_results,\nviper_results)
activate DM
DM -> DM: Group by vector ID
DM -> DM: Select newest version\nby timestamp
DM -> DM: Sort by relevance score
DM --> VS: Final deduplicated results
deactivate DM

VS -> VS: Apply result limit (top-k)
VS -> VS: Format response with\nrequested fields

VS --> H: Search results (JSON/Proto)
deactivate VS

H -> H: Add metrics & timing
H --> C: HTTP 200 OK\n{results, metrics}
deactivate H

== Error Handling ==

alt Collection Not Found
  VS --> H: Error: Collection not found
  H --> C: HTTP 404 Not Found
end

alt Timeout Exceeded
  VS --> H: Error: Search timeout
  H --> C: HTTP 408 Request Timeout
end

note over SF
  SearchEngineFactory selects:
  - MemoryOnlyEngine (WAL only)
  - LsmEngine (WAL + LSM)
  - ViperEngine (WAL + VIPER)
  - HybridEngine (All tiers)
end note

note over VIPER
  Two-stage search:
  1. Coarse: INT8/PQ quantized
  2. Fine: FP32 reranking
end note

@enduml